125
00:05:21,694 --> 00:05:24,710
One thing to know about printk
is you might be concerned,

126
00:05:24,710 --> 00:05:27,290
well, what if I'm
taking an interrupt?

127
00:05:27,290 --> 00:05:29,225
Do I need to worry about

128
00:05:29,225 --> 00:05:31,700
an interrupt happening and
trying to write from printk,

129
00:05:31,700 --> 00:05:33,020
will there be something
that it's doing

130
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:34,715
that's not safe to
do an interrupt.

131
00:05:34,715 --> 00:05:37,190
It turns out that this is
basically design a printk.

132
00:05:37,190 --> 00:05:39,080
The print's not actually written

133
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:41,525
anywhere as a part of
your call to printk,

134
00:05:41,525 --> 00:05:44,210
it's just written into
a circular buffer.

135
00:05:44,210 --> 00:05:45,860
Then there's another
task that comes out

136
00:05:45,860 --> 00:05:47,360
