the circular buffer

137
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:51,140
and actually writes it out
to someplace like a file.

138
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:55,684
That means that it's safe
to use printk anywhere,

139
00:05:55,684 --> 00:05:58,500
including in interrupt handlers.

140
00:05:59,620 --> 00:06:03,005
A lot of times you end up in
a situation where you've got

141
00:06:03,005 --> 00:06:04,310
Debug prints that are going to

